      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to convert each repeating decimal into its fractional form and then perform the subtraction. Here's the step-by-step solution:\n\n1. Convert the repeating decimals to fractions.\n\nLet's start with \\(0.\\overline{789}\\):\n\nLet \\( x = 0.\\overline{789} \\).\n\nThen, \\( 1000x = 789.\\overline{789} \\).\n\nSubtracting these two equations, we get:\n\\[ 1000x - x = 789.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{789} \\]\n\\[ 999x = 789 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{789}{999} \\]\n\nNext, let's convert \\(0.\\overline{456}\\) to a fraction:\n\nLet \\( y = 0.\\overline{456} \\).\n\nThen, \\( 1000y = 456.\\overline{456} \\).\n\nSubtracting these two equations, we get:\n\\[ 1000y - y = 456.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{456} \\]\n\\[ 999y = 456 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{456}{999} \\]\n\nFinally, let's convert \\(0.\\overline{123}\\) to a fraction:\n\nLet \\( z = 0.\\overline{123} \\).\n\nThen, \\( 1000z = 123.\\overline{123} \\).\n\nSubtracting these two equations, we get:\n\\[ 1000z - z = 123.\\overline{123} - 0.\\overline{123} \\]\n\\[ 999z = 123 \\]\n\\[ z = \\frac{123}{999} \\]\n\n2. Now, we need to find \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\):\n\n\\[\n0.\\overline{789} = \\frac{789}{999}, \\quad 0.\\overline{456} = \\frac{456}{999}, \\quad 0.\\overline{123} = \\frac{123}{999}\n\\]\n\nSo, we need to subtract the individual fractions:\n\n\\[\n0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123} = \\frac{789}{999} - \\frac{456}{999} - \\frac{123}{999}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{789 - 456 - 123}{999} = \\frac{789 - 579}{999} = \\frac{210}{999}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we need to simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{210}{999}\\) to its lowest terms. Let's use Python to simplify this fraction.\n```python\nfrom math import gcd\n\n# Numerator and denominator of the fraction\nnumerator = 210\ndenominator = 999\n\n# Compute the greatest common divisor (gcd)\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, denominator)\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nsimplified_